  "notes": "Three parameters carry this entry and all three are named in the research. (1) **The whole-tone lead.** \"Occasional whole-tone-flavoured lead lines\" is the only place in this batch a symmetric scale is authored; it sits at weight 1 of 9, which is what \"occasional\" means, and it is the reason `melody.register` reaches 100 — a whole-tone line has nowhere to resolve, so it stays up where it reads as colour. (2) **The open hat on the last 8th.** \"Open-hat accents on the last 8th of the bar\" is `openHat.prob` 0.55 on `4&` alone — the highest open-hat rate in this batch, and the one gesture that makes this beat identifiable in a bar. (3) **A staccato 808.** \"Bouncy short-decay 808 with fast repeated notes and 16th-note glides; more staccato than the Jeezy/Waka lineage\" is `sustain: staccato` in the highest 808 register here, which is the direct opposite of the two entries the research names. \"Single high bell/marimba motif, 2-bar loop, 4–6 pitch set, no pad; sparse mid-range by design\" is `motifPitchCount` 5 with `chords.impliedByRiff` — the loop is unchanged throughout, so the chord part's variety comes from duration and voicing rather than from motion. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` — chart and era are solid, production detail is generalized from the released catalog. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the kick's 0.6 `syncopation` for \"16th-syncopated\", the family weights, and the whole `intervals`/`contour` split. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
